# Build context for backend/Dockerfile is the REPOSITORY ROOT, not ./backend, so
# that scripts/ ships inside the image. That makes this file a security control
# rather than only a size control: everything is excluded by default and only the
# two directories the image actually needs are re-included.
#
# This supersedes backend/.dockerignore, which is no longer consulted — Docker
# reads only the file at the root of the build context.
#
# Rules are last-match-wins, so the re-includes come first and the exclusions
# that protect them come after.

# 1. Exclude everything.
**

# 2. Re-include what the Dockerfile copies. Parent directories must be
#    un-excluded before their children, or Docker never descends into them.
!backend
!backend/**
!scripts
!scripts/**

# 3. Never bake these in, even under a re-included directory.
#    Secrets first: .env files hold live database credentials and API keys.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.key
**/*.pem

# Dependencies and build artefacts — enormous, and never needed at runtime.
backend/.venv
backend/env
backend/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/node_modules
**/build
**/dist
**/*.egg-info

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.log
